<h3 data-start=3D"1407" data-end=3D"1458" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1411" data-end=3D"1458">1. Introduction au cycle de vie d=E2=80=99un widget=
</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"1460" data-end=3D"1504" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1465" data-end=3D"1504">Qu=E2=80=99est-ce qu=E2=80=99un Widget en Flutter ?=
</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"1506" data-end=3D"1710" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"1509" data-end=3D"1519">Widget</strong> est l=E2=80=99unit=C3=A9 de bas=
e de l=E2=80=99interface utilisateur (UI) dans Flutter. Tout, depuis les bo=
utons jusqu'aux animations, est un widget. Dans Flutter, il existe principa=
lement deux types de widgets :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1711" data-end=3D"2056">
<li data-start=3D"1711" data-end=3D"1861" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1713" data-end=3D"1861" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
713" data-end=3D"1734">Stateless Widgets</strong> : Ce sont des widgets qui=
 n'ont pas d'=C3=A9tat interne. Leur apparence est fig=C3=A9e, elle ne chan=
ge jamais apr=C3=A8s leur initialisation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1862" data-end=3D"2056" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1864" data-end=3D"2056" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
864" data-end=3D"1884">Stateful Widgets</strong> : Ce sont des widgets qui =
poss=C3=A8dent un =C3=A9tat mutable. Leur apparence peut changer pendant le=
ur cycle de vie en fonction des actions de l=E2=80=99utilisateur ou d=E2=80=
=99autres =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2058" data-end=3D"2183" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"2061" data-end=3D"2089">cycle de vie des widgets</strong> se r=C3=A9f=
=C3=A8re aux diff=C3=A9rentes =C3=A9tapes durant lesquelles un widget est c=
r=C3=A9=C3=A9, mis =C3=A0 jour ou d=C3=A9truit.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2185" data-end=3D"2188" class=3D"">
<h3 data-start=3D"2190" data-end=3D"2238" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2194" data-end=3D"2238">2. Le cycle de vie d=E2=80=99un <code data-start=3D=
"2220" data-end=3D"2236">StatefulWidget</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2240" data-end=3D"2519" class=3D"">Les <code data-start=3D=
"2244" data-end=3D"2261">StatefulWidgets</code> ont un cycle de vie beaucou=
p plus riche que les <code data-start=3D"2310" data-end=3D"2328">StatelessW=
idgets</code> car ils maintiennent un =C3=A9tat qui peut changer. Lorsqu=E2=
=80=99un <code data-start=3D"2386" data-end=3D"2402">StatefulWidget</code> =
est ins=C3=A9r=C3=A9 dans l=E2=80=99arbre des widgets, il cr=C3=A9e un <str=
ong data-start=3D"2451" data-end=3D"2460">State</strong> (=C3=A9tat), et ce=
t =C3=A9tat g=C3=A8re les changements dans l=E2=80=99interface.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"2521" data-end=3D"2560" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2526" data-end=3D"2560">Cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99un <code data-start=3D"2542=
" data-end=3D"2558">StatefulWidget</code></strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2562" data-end=3D"2610" class=3D"">Un <code data-start=3D"=
2565" data-end=3D"2581">StatefulWidget</code> se compose de deux classes :<=
/p>
<ol data-start=3D"2611" data-end=3D"2818">
<li data-start=3D"2611" data-end=3D"2723" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2614" data-end=3D"2723" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
614" data-end=3D"2644">La classe <code data-start=3D"2626" data-end=3D"2642=
">StatefulWidget</code></strong> : qui est le widget lui-m=C3=AAme et qui c=
ontient la logique de cr=C3=A9ation de l'=C3=A9tat.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2724" data-end=3D"2818" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2727" data-end=3D"2818" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
727" data-end=3D"2748">La classe <code data-start=3D"2739" data-end=3D"2746=
">State</code></strong> : qui contient l'=C3=A9tat du widget et qui g=C3=A8=
re les mises =C3=A0 jour de l'UI.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2820" data-end=3D"2857" class=3D"">Exemple de base de <cod=
e data-start=3D"2839" data-end=3D"2855">StatefulWidget</code> :</p>
