<h3 data-start=3D"2443" data-end=3D"2494" class=3D"">1. <strong data-start=
=3D"2450" data-end=3D"2494">Introduction =C3=A0 la programmation r=C3=A9act=
ive</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"2496" data-end=3D"2546" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2501" data-end=3D"2546">Qu'est-ce que la programmation r=C3=A9active ?</str=
ong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"2548" data-end=3D"2854" class=3D"">La programmation r=C3=
=A9active est un paradigme qui permet de traiter des flux de donn=C3=A9es q=
ui peuvent =C3=AAtre observ=C3=A9s, =C3=A9cout=C3=A9s, et transform=C3=A9s =
de mani=C3=A8re r=C3=A9active. Le but est de r=C3=A9agir aux changements d'=
=C3=A9tat ou aux =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements en temps r=C3=A9el sans avoir =C3=A0 =
g=C3=A9rer manuellement le changement de l'=C3=A9tat de l'application.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2856" data-end=3D"3020" class=3D"">Les flux de donn=C3=A9e=
s sont g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement repr=C3=A9sent=C3=A9s par des <strong data-st=
art=3D"2914" data-end=3D"2925">Streams</strong>, et les composants de l'app=
lication qui "=C3=A9coutent" ces flux sont appel=C3=A9s des <strong data-st=
art=3D"3003" data-end=3D"3019">observateurs</strong>.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"3022" data-end=3D"3076" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3027" data-end=3D"3076">Pourquoi utiliser la programmation r=C3=A9active ?<=
/strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3078" data-end=3D"3292" class=3D"">La programmation r=C3=
=A9active est particuli=C3=A8rement utile dans des applications o=C3=B9 il =
est n=C3=A9cessaire de r=C3=A9agir =C3=A0 des =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements qui se p=
roduisent en dehors du contr=C3=B4le imm=C3=A9diat du programme. Quelques e=
xemples incluent :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3293" data-end=3D"3638">
<li data-start=3D"3293" data-end=3D"3391" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3295" data-end=3D"3391" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
295" data-end=3D"3332">Interfaces utilisateur dynamiques</strong> o=C3=B9 l=
'=C3=A9tat change en fonction des actions de l'utilisateur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3392" data-end=3D"3502" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3394" data-end=3D"3502" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
394" data-end=3D"3461">Applications web ou mobiles avec des mises =C3=A0 jo=
ur en temps r=C3=A9el</strong> (ex. chat en ligne, notifications push).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3503" data-end=3D"3638" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3505" data-end=3D"3638" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
505" data-end=3D"3578">Applications qui traitent de grandes quantit=C3=A9s =
de donn=C3=A9es asynchrones</strong>, telles que les applications de stream=
ing ou de monitoring.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3640" data-end=3D"3699" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3645" data-end=3D"3699">Principe de base : Flux de donn=C3=A9es et observat=
eurs</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"3701" data-end=3D"3826" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99id=C3=A9e cen=
trale est de travailler avec des flux de donn=C3=A9es et des observateurs q=
ui r=C3=A9agissent =C3=A0 ces flux. En termes simples :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3827" data-end=3D"4080">
<li data-start=3D"3827" data-end=3D"3960" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3829" data-end=3D"3960" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"3832" data-end=3D"3851">Flux de donn=C3=A9es</strong> (Stream) est une =
s=C3=A9quence de valeurs (donn=C3=A9es) qui peuvent =C3=AAtre envoy=C3=A9es=
 =C3=A0 diff=C3=A9rents moments dans le temps.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3961" data-end=3D"4080" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3963" data-end=3D"4080" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"3966" data-end=3D"3981">Observateur</strong> est un objet ou un composa=
nt qui "=C3=A9coute" un flux de donn=C3=A9es pour r=C3=A9agir =C3=A0 chaque=
 nouvelle valeur.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4082" data-end=3D"4141" class=3D"">2. <strong data-start=
=3D"4089" data-end=3D"4141">Les bases de la programmation r=C3=A9active ave=
c Dart</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"4143" data-end=3D"4171" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4148" data-end=3D"4171">Les Streams en Dart</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"4173" data-end=3D"4310" class=3D"">En Dart, le <strong dat=
a-start=3D"4185" data-end=3D"4195">Stream</strong> est une s=C3=A9quence de=
 donn=C3=A9es qui arrive au fil du temps. Le <strong data-start=3D"4255" da=
ta-end=3D"4265">Stream</strong> peut =C3=A9mettre des =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements =
de trois types :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4311" data-end=3D"4498">
<li data-start=3D"4311" data-end=3D"4370" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4313" data-end=3D"4370" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
313" data-end=3D"4338">=C3=89v=C3=A9nements de donn=C3=A9es</strong> : Vale=
urs envoy=C3=A9es par le flux.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4371" data-end=3D"4436" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4373" data-end=3D"4436" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
373" data-end=3D"4383">Erreur</strong> : En cas de probl=C3=A8me pendant l'=
envoi des =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4437" data-end=3D"4498" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4439" data-end=3D"4498" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
439" data-end=3D"4452">Fermeture</strong> : Signale la fin de la s=C3=A9que=
nce d'=C3=A9v=C3=A9nements.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4500" data-end=3D"4547" class=3D"">Dart fournit deux types=
 principaux de Streams :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4548" data-end=3D"4701">
<li data-start=3D"4548" data-end=3D"4626" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4550" data-end=3D"4626" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
550" data-end=3D"4568">Unicast Stream</strong> : Un flux auquel un seul abo=
nn=C3=A9 peut s'abonner =C3=A0 la fois.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4627" data-end=3D"4701" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4629" data-end=3D"4701" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
629" data-end=3D"4649">Broadcast Stream</strong> : Un flux auquel plusieurs=
 abonn=C3=A9s peuvent =C3=A9couter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4703" data-end=3D"4740" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4708" data-end=3D"4740">Le concept de Sink et Stream</strong></h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4742" data-end=3D"4989">
<li data-start=3D"4742" data-end=3D"4865" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4744" data-end=3D"4865" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"4747" data-end=3D"4755">Sink</strong> est un objet vers lequel on envoi=
e des =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements. Vous pouvez l'imaginer comme un "producteur" d'=
=C3=A9v=C3=A9nements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4866" data-end=3D"4989" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4868" data-end=3D"4989" class=3D"">Un <strong data-start=
=3D"4871" data-end=3D"4881">Stream</strong> est l'objet qui diffuse ces =C3=
=A9v=C3=A9nements. Il agit comme un "consommateur" des =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements=
 envoy=C3=A9s par le Sink.</p>
</li>
</ul>
